Privacy Policy — Debt Notes

​Effective Date: October 2026

App Name: Debt Notes

Package Name: org.notes.debt

Version: 1.3.7

Developer: Mahi Yadav (rumahiyadav)

​Your debts, expenses, and financial records — all in one place.

​This Privacy Policy explains how Debt Notes (com.notes.debt) handles your information when you use the application.

​1. Local & Offline Data Storage

​Debt Notes is a 100% offline personal notebook application.

​All information you enter into the app—including names, debt amounts, expense entries, notes, reminder dates, and optional proof images—is stored exclusively on your device inside the app's private local storage.

​Debt Notes does not request the Android INTERNET permission. 

​We do not operate remote servers or cloud databases, and we never collect, transmit, sell, or share your personal or financial data with any third party.

​The app contains no third-party analytics SDKs, tracking scripts, or advertising networks.

​2. Permissions Used

​Debt Notes requests only the device permissions necessary for features you choose to use:

Permission

```Purpose```

Notifications (POST_NOTIFICATIONS)

```Used solely to display local reminder alerts when a scheduled debt reminder time arrives.```

Exact Alarms (USE_EXACT_ALARM, SCHEDULE_EXACT_ALARM)

```Used to trigger your scheduled payment or collection reminders at the exact date and time you select.```

Boot Completed (RECEIVE_BOOT_COMPLETED)

```Used to restore your active scheduled reminders after your phone restarts.```

Camera & Photo Picker (CAMERA)

```Optional. Used only when you choose to take or attach a proof photo or receipt to a note.```


3. Backups & Data Sharing

​Debt Notes includes a built-in Backup / Export and Share backup tool in Settings. 

​Portable JSON backup files (debt-notes-backup.json) are created or shared only when you manually initiate an export or share action using Android's system file picker or share sheet. 

​You are in full control of where your exported backup files are stored or shared.

​4. Data Retention & Deletion

​Your records remain on your device for as long as you choose to keep them.

​You can edit or delete any debt note, expense sheet, or attached proof image at any time directly inside the app.

​Uninstalling the application or clearing the app's storage in your device settings permanently deletes all locally stored app data, except for any JSON backup files you have manually exported to your device storage.

​5. Children's Privacy

​Debt Notes does not collect or transmit personal data from any user of any age, including children.

​6. Changes to This Privacy Policy

​If we update this Privacy Policy in future versions of Debt Notes, the revised policy will be posted on this page with an updated effective date.

